<Defs>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       THE ORBITAL GATE

       More Realistic Research (sae.ResearchMod) makes physical materials a
       hard prerequisite for a named research project. Its own readme:

         "Any research projects (vanilla or modded) that are not listed in
          this file will automatically generate their own analysis
          requirements based on their Tech Level."

       Anything we DO list overrides that default. So by naming every
       glittertech project and demanding glitterhearts - an item that exists
       only in orbit and cannot be crafted or bought - the whole tree becomes
       impossible to finish from the ground.

       This is the mechanism that makes space mandatory rather than merely
       rewarding. Ushanka's own gating is just craftable benches; without
       this file you can research the entire glittertech tree and never
       leave the planet.

       COSTS ARE TIERED by depth in their tech tree:
         1 heart  - foundation and the cheaper utility branches
         2 hearts - fabrication, panels, the heavy/alchemy line
         3 hearts - the resurrector, the deepest project in the mod

       Each entry also lists a cheap secondary material so the analysis has
       something to consume besides the heart itself. Reverse-engineering a
       glitterheart is the gate; the rest is busywork that reads as lab time.

       If this proves too punishing, lower the pointsRequired values before
       removing hearts - the number of hearts is the story, the points are
       the grind.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <!-- ============ Foundation ============ -->

  <ResearchMakesSense.ManualAnalysisDef>
    <defName>Archinity_GT_Fabrication</defName>
    <researchProject>USH_GlittertechFabrication</researchProject>
    <reverseEngineeringMaterials>
      <li>Archinity_Glitterheart</li>
    </reverseEngineeringMaterials>
    <reverseEngineeringPointsRequired>2</reverseEngineeringPointsRequired>
    <theoreticalMaterials>
      <li>ComponentSpacer</li>
    </theoreticalMaterials>
    <theoreticalPointsRequired>8</theoreticalPointsRequired>
  </ResearchMakesSense.ManualAnalysisDef>

